#, no-wrap
msgid "Leverage trim SQD for improved configuration selection for the latest version of Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD)"
msgstr "Gamitin ang trim SQD para sa mas pinahusay na pagpili ng configuration para sa pinakabagong bersyon ng Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD)"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Leverage trim SQD for improved configuration selection"
msgstr "Gamitin ang trim SQD para sa mas pinahusay na pagpili ng configuration"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/trim-sqd.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The default behavior of [`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion) is to diagonalize each subsampled batch and keep the best result. **Trim SQD** instead treats the batches as candidates to be screened: each is diagonalized, *trimmed* down to the configurations carrying the largest weight, and the survivors of all the batches are merged and diagonalized together. That merged diagonalization is the one whose energy the iteration reports, and its own trimmed output seeds the next iteration.\n"
msgstr "Ang default na gawi ng [`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion) ay i-diagonalize ang bawat na-subsample na batch at panatilihin ang pinakamahusay na resulta. Sa halip, tinatrato ng **Trim SQD** ang mga batch bilang mga kandidatong sasalain: bawat isa ay dinadiagonalize, *tinatrim* hanggang sa mga configuration na may pinakamalaking weight, at ang mga nakaligtas mula sa lahat ng batch ay pinagsasama at dinadiagonalize nang sama-sama. Ang pinagsamang diagonalization na iyon ang may energy na iuulat ng iteration, at ang sarili nitong trimmed na output ang nagiging binhi ng susunod na iteration.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The trim SQD implementation is based on joint research from\n"
"the Cleveland Clinic Foundation, RIKEN, and IBM&reg;. If you use this feature in\n"
"your research, also cite the paper. You can find the citation in the\n"
"`CITATION.bib` file, with citation key `merz2026crossing`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang trim SQD na implementasyon ay batay sa magkasanib na pananaliksik mula sa\n"
"Cleveland Clinic Foundation, RIKEN, at IBM&reg;. Kung gagamitin mo ang feature na ito sa\n"
"iyong pananaliksik, banggitin din ang papel. Makikita mo ang citation sa\n"
"file na `CITATION.bib`, na may citation key na `merz2026crossing`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For more details on the SQD code used in this example, see the [chemistry Hamiltonian tutorial](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization).\n"
msgstr "Para sa higit pang detalye tungkol sa SQD code na ginamit sa halimbawang ito, tingnan ang [tutorial ng chemistry Hamiltonian](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up the molecule {#set-up-the-molecule}"
msgstr "I-set up ang molecule {#set-up-the-molecule}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the loop {#run-the-loop}"
msgstr "Patakbuhin ang loop {#run-the-loop}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One trim SQD iteration does the following:\n"
msgstr "Ganito ang ginagawa ng isang trim SQD iteration:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Screening round.** Partition the bitstrings into batches.  Diagonalize each batch and keep the `trim_ratio` fraction of its CI strings, per spin sector, ranked by weight.\n"
msgstr "**Screening round.** Hatiin ang mga bitstring sa mga batch.  I-diagonalize ang bawat batch at panatilihin ang fraction na `trim_ratio` ng mga CI string nito, bawat spin sector, na niraranggo ayon sa weight.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Merged round.** Diagonalize the merged survivors once. This is the result the iteration reports, and its own trimmed strings seed the next iteration.\n"
msgstr "**Merged round.** I-diagonalize nang isang beses ang pinagsamang mga nakaligtas. Ito ang resultang iuulat ng iteration, at ang sarili nitong trimmed na mga string ang nagiging binhi ng susunod na iteration.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The loop's `sci_solver` performs both rounds, and defaults to this package's PySCF solver.\n"
msgstr "Ang `sci_solver` ng loop ang gumagawa ng parehong round, at ang default nito ay ang PySCF solver ng package na ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Enable trim SQD by passing the `TrimPolicy` as follows:\n"
msgstr "I-enable ang trim SQD sa pamamagitan ng pagpasa ng `TrimPolicy` tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check whether screening is helping {#check-whether-screening-is-helping}"
msgstr "Tingnan kung nakakatulong ang screening {#check-whether-screening-is-helping}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Screening has the most to offer when the sampled configurations greatly outnumber what can be diagonalized at once, so that ranking a larger pool genuinely finds configurations a single batch would have missed. It has the least to offer when a subspace of the affordable size already captures most of the wavefunction.\n"
msgstr "Pinakamalaki ang naitutulong ng screening kapag mas marami nang malaki ang mga na-sample na configuration kaysa sa kayang i-diagonalize nang sabay-sabay, kaya ang pagraranggo sa mas malaking pool ay talagang nakakahanap ng mga configuration na hindi mapapansin ng isang batch lang. Pinakamaliit naman ang naitutulong nito kapag ang subspace na may abot-kayang laki ay nakukuha na ang karamihan ng wavefunction.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Screening depends on the batches differing from one another. `TrimPolicy` manages this by modifying the behavior of `diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian` to draw one pool of `samples_per_batch * num_batches` bitstrings and partitioning it among the batches, so no bitstring appears in more than one.\n"
msgstr "Nakadepende ang screening sa pagkakaiba ng mga batch sa isa't isa. Pinamamahalaan ito ng `TrimPolicy` sa pamamagitan ng pagbabago sa gawi ng `diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian` para kumuha ng isang pool ng `samples_per_batch * num_batches` na mga bitstring at hatiin ito sa mga batch, kaya walang bitstring na lumalabas sa higit sa isang batch.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bound the subspace {#bound-the-subspace}"
msgstr "Limitahan ang subspace {#bound-the-subspace}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A subspace here is spanned by the *Cartesian product* of a spin-alpha and a spin-beta CI string array.\n"
msgstr "Ang isang subspace dito ay binubuo ng *Cartesian product* ng isang spin-alpha at isang spin-beta na CI string array.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trimming ranks configurations, but the carryover is two per-spin string lists. Keeping the 150 highest-weight configurations of a subspace typically involves close to 150 distinct alpha strings and 150 distinct beta strings, whose product spans roughly 22,500 configurations, not 150. So the subspace handed to the next iteration is generally much larger than the set that was ranked, and it grows quadratically in what you retain.\n"
msgstr "Niraranggo ng trimming ang mga configuration, pero ang carryover ay dalawang listahan ng string bawat spin. Ang pagpapanatili sa 150 configuration na may pinakamataas na weight ng isang subspace ay karaniwang nangangailangan ng malapit sa 150 natatanging alpha string at 150 natatanging beta string, na ang product ay sumasaklaw sa humigit-kumulang 22,500 configuration, hindi 150. Kaya ang subspace na ipinapasa sa susunod na iteration ay karaniwang mas malaki nang husto kaysa sa set na niraranggo, at lumalaki ito nang quadratic sa dami ng pinapanatili mo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trimming and carrying over are bounded separately, because they happen at different points: trimming shrinks each batch of the screening round, while the carryover is what crosses into the next iteration.\n"
msgstr "Magkahiwalay ang limitasyon ng trimming at carryover, dahil nangyayari ang mga ito sa magkaibang punto: pinaliliit ng trimming ang bawat batch ng screening round, habang ang carryover ang tumatawid papunta sa susunod na iteration.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Four arguments bound it, and it is useful to set at least one:\n"
msgstr "Apat na argument ang naglilimita rito, at kapaki-pakinabang na mag-set ng kahit isa:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`trim_ratio`** is the fraction of each batch's strings, per spin sector, that survive screening. Lower values shrink the merged subspace but discard configurations the next iteration must rediscover by sampling.\n"
msgstr "Ang **`trim_ratio`** ay ang fraction ng mga string ng bawat batch, bawat spin sector, na nakakaligtas sa screening. Pinaliliit ng mas mababang value ang pinagsamang subspace pero itinatapon nito ang mga configuration na kailangang matuklasang muli ng susunod na iteration sa pamamagitan ng sampling.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`max_strings_per_trim`** caps the strings each batch contributes, per sector, regardless of the ratio. Useful with `symmetrize_spin`, which merges both spin sectors into one list and so roughly doubles what each batch offers. This bound is **per batch**: the merged subspace can hold up to `num_batches` times as many strings, less whatever the batches had in common, which in practice is not much.\n"
msgstr "Nililimitahan ng **`max_strings_per_trim`** ang mga string na naiaambag ng bawat batch, bawat sector, anuman ang ratio. Kapaki-pakinabang ito kasama ang `symmetrize_spin`, na pinagsasama ang parehong spin sector sa isang listahan kaya halos nadodoble ang iniaalok ng bawat batch. Ang limitasyong ito ay **bawat batch**: ang pinagsamang subspace ay maaaring maglaman ng hanggang `num_batches` beses na mas maraming string, bawas ang anumang pinagsaluhan ng mga batch, na sa praktika ay hindi gaanong marami.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`carryover_threshold`**, **`carryover_ratio`**, and **`max_carryover`** bound the strings that seed the next iteration, applied to the merged subspace as a whole rather than per batch. `carryover_threshold` is the amplitude cutoff that `StandardPolicy` uses, with the same default; the other two bound the count, which the cutoff alone does not.\n"
msgstr "Nililimitahan ng **`carryover_threshold`**, **`carryover_ratio`**, at **`max_carryover`** ang mga string na nagiging binhi ng susunod na iteration, na inilalapat sa pinagsamang subspace sa kabuuan sa halip na bawat batch. Ang `carryover_threshold` ay ang amplitude cutoff na ginagamit ng `StandardPolicy`, na may parehong default; ang dalawa pa ay naglilimita sa bilang, na hindi nagagawa ng cutoff lang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`max_dim`**, on `diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian` itself, bounds each spin sector of every subspace the loop diagonalizes, including the merged one. It acts as a backstop and applies to whatever the policy returns, after the carryover is merged with fresh samples.\n"
msgstr "Nililimitahan ng **`max_dim`**, sa mismong `diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian`, ang bawat spin sector ng bawat subspace na dinadiagonalize ng loop, kasama ang pinagsama. Gumaganap itong backstop at inilalapat sa anumang ibinabalik ng policy, pagkatapos pagsamahin ang carryover sa mga bagong sample.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The run above sets `max_strings_per_trim=250` and `max_dim=250` together, so neither what each batch contributes nor the subspace built from it can run away.\n"
msgstr "Itinatakda ng run sa itaas ang `max_strings_per_trim=250` at `max_dim=250` nang magkasama, kaya hindi lalampas sa hangganan ang naiaambag ng bawat batch ni ang subspace na binuo mula rito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use an external eigensolver {#use-an-external-eigensolver}"
msgstr "Gumamit ng external na eigensolver {#use-an-external-eigensolver}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can use trim SQD with an external eigensolver by passing the `sci_solver` argument:\n"
msgstr "Magagamit mo ang trim SQD kasama ang isang external na eigensolver sa pamamagitan ng pagpasa ng argument na `sci_solver`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The prior snippet requires the `sbd-eigensolver` package to be installed from PyPI.\n"
msgstr "Kailangang naka-install mula sa PyPI ang package na `sbd-eigensolver` para sa naunang snippet.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Distribute the work {#distribute-the-work}"
msgstr "Ipamahagi ang gawain {#distribute-the-work}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With `TrimPolicy`, the loop calls `sci_solver` twice per iteration: once with all the batches, and once with the merged subspace. Both calls go through the ordinary `sci_solver` interface, which [this package's multi-process support](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/hpc-acceleration) invokes collectively on every MPI rank.\n"
msgstr "Sa `TrimPolicy`, dalawang beses tinatawag ng loop ang `sci_solver` bawat iteration: minsan kasama ang lahat ng batch, at minsan kasama ang pinagsamang subspace. Parehong dumadaan ang dalawang tawag sa karaniwang interface ng `sci_solver`, na kolektibong tinatawag ng [multi-process support ng package na ito](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/hpc-acceleration) sa bawat MPI rank.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two levels of parallelism are potentially available, and they are independent:\n"
msgstr "Dalawang antas ng parallelism ang posibleng magamit, at hiwalay ang mga ito sa isa't isa:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Within a diagonalization.** A solver such as SBD can spread a single diagonalization across ranks.\n"
msgstr "**Sa loob ng isang diagonalization.** Ang isang solver tulad ng SBD ay maaaring ipamahagi ang isang diagonalization sa mga rank.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Across the batches.** A solver could, in principle, diagonalize the batches concurrently.\n"
msgstr "**Sa iba't ibang batch.** Ang isang solver ay maaari, sa prinsipyo, na i-diagonalize nang sabay-sabay ang mga batch.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Given a set of batches, the solver determines how to delegate work to its worker processes.\n"
msgstr "Kapag may set ng mga batch, ang solver ang magpapasya kung paano ipapasa ang gawain sa mga worker process nito.\n"
